  "answer": "I found no earlier ticket that reports this problem. The closest one, WSL#40944, is a different issue. In that ticket every wslc command failed with E_INVALIDARG because of a bug in how the session name was generated from a Windows username containing a '.'. In your case pull and save work, and only `wslc image import` without a tag fails. Until this is fixed, give the image an explicit tag, for example `wslc image import alp.tar test:latest`, which you've already confirmed works. Please keep this ticket open as a bug report. The expected behavior is that a missing tag defaults to :latest, as it does with `docker import`."
 },
